# Publish commits and pushes after packaging

After a successful production package (`./deploy/publish.sh`, not `--dry-run`):

1. Commit any remaining local changes if the working tree is dirty.
2. `git push` the current branch to GitHub (`origin`).
3. Continue the server release using that commit.

`--allow-dirty` is accepted for compatibility; leftover files are still committed after packaging. `--dry-run` must not commit or push.
